[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read report by report, it
holds three problems. One fix will not close it.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket, and its own fix.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

Every report is counted once: the ticket export repeats some reports where its pages overlap.

## How to tell them apart

- **Parser.** The date has its day and month swapped, whatever channel it came in by. The
  tenant writes day first; the shared parser reads month first. Fixing the parser fixes these.
- **booking-v3 hint.** Also a swap, but only from tenants on `booking-v3`, and only through its
  form. The form's hint asks for `MM/DD/YYYY`, people follow it, and the form reads their date
  day first. Fixing the parser does not fix these: the hint is the bug.
- **One-day move.** Not a swap. The day moves by one (Tuesday shows as Monday), or two people
  in different time zones get different days for one meeting. The desk had already noted these
  reports; the cause table files them under the parser by tenant, so they had no ticket.

## Why one ticket hid three

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match.
Reporters write the same few subjects for all three problems, so subject matching put them in
one place. Intake's tag does not help either: it guesses from the reporter's browser, and the
cause depends on the tenant and the form.

The table on the incident page shows the same split by cause, with the one-day moves left
inside the parser row:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes for the desk

- Close #4471 only when all three tickets are closed.
- When a report's dates are not a swap, check the time zone before merging it.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
